NON-COMMERCIAL SOFTWARE LICENSE AGREEMENT
1. Definitions

a. "Software" means the software application known as [Software Name], including all its components, source code, and documentation. b. "Non-Commercial Use" means use of the Software for personal, private, non-profit educational, or internal research purposes only. Non-Commercial Use does not include any activity that is directly or indirectly intended for or directed towards commercial advantage or monetary compensation. c. "Commercial Use" means any use of the Software in connection with a business, organization, or venture for profit, including, but not limited to, providing services for a fee, selling products, or using the Software as an integral part of a commercial workflow.

2. License Grant and Restriction

a. The Licensor grants you a limited, non-exclusive, revocable license to use, copy, and modify the Software strictly for Non-Commercial Use only. b. You may not use the Software for any Commercial Use unless you have executed a separate, written Commercial License Agreement with the Licensor. Any use of the Software for Commercial Use without a valid Commercial License is a breach of this Agreement and grounds for immediate termination.

3. Termination of License

a. Automatic Termination. This License is automatically terminated, without notice from the Licensor, if you breach any term of this Agreement, including, but not limited to, using the Software for Commercial Use in violation of Section 2(b). b. Effect of Termination. Upon termination, you must immediately cease all use of the Software, and destroy all copies, modifications, and derivative works of the Software in your possession or control.

4. Remedies for Breach (Liquidated Damages)

a. Violation as Copyright Infringement. You acknowledge that the Software is protected by copyright law and that any use of the Software outside the scope of this Non-Commercial License constitutes both a breach of this Agreement and copyright infringement. b. Liquidated Damages for Commercial Use. You acknowledge and agree that damages resulting from the unauthorized Commercial Use of the Software would be difficult to calculate, as such unauthorized use deprives the Licensor of the opportunity to negotiate a commercial license fee and causes unquantifiable harm to the Licensor's commercial strategy. c. Pre-Agreed Compensation. Therefore, you agree that if you use the Software for Commercial Use without first obtaining a separate written Commercial License from the Licensor, you shall pay the Licensor the sum of ˆ100,000 (One Hundred Thousand Euros) as liquidated damages for each instance or occurrence of unauthorized Commercial Use, or as a lump sum for any continuous unauthorized Commercial Use. d. Not a Penalty. You agree that this sum represents a reasonable and genuine pre-estimate of the loss and damage the Licensor would suffer due to the breach and is not intended as a penalty. e. Right to Further Remedies. Payment of liquidated damages under this Section 4(c) does not limit the Licensor's right to pursue other remedies available under law, including, but not limited to, seeking injunctive relief (a court order to stop the infringement), or pursuing actual damages if those damages exceed the amount of liquidated damages.